fpac (4.1.5-rc16)

	* wp/fpacwpd.c: let poll_adjacents() recover an adjacent connection
	  that hangs while being established.  poll_adjacents() only retried
	  adjacents in the DISCONNECTED state; a non-blocking ROSE connect
	  that completed neither successfully (no write event) nor with an
	  error stayed in WPA_CONNECTING forever, leaving the node isolated
	  with no White Pages session until fpacwpd was restarted by hand.
	  retry_connect_date, already armed to now+120 s by connect_adjacent(),
	  is now honoured in the CONNECTING state as well: a connect still
	  pending after that delay is closed, which returns the adjacent to
	  DISCONNECTED and reschedules a retry, so the daemon heals itself.

	* lib/libwp.c, wp/fpacwpd.c: stop an obsolete deleted record from
	  tearing down a whole adjacent session.  The wire codec rejected a
	  deleted record older than WP_OBSOLETE by returning -1, both when
	  sending (wp_send_pdu) and when receiving (wp_receive_pdu); the
	  daemon read that -1 as a fatal link error and called close_client(),
	  so a single stale deletion crossing the link dropped the session and
	  the nodes reconnected in a loop.  The obsolescence policy is moved
	  out of the codec and into the daemon: wp_send_pdu() and
	  wp_receive_pdu() now only encode and decode the is_deleted flag,
	  while rose_read_handler() skips an obsolete deleted record (mirroring
	  the existing send-side skip) and keeps the session up.  The policy
	  itself is unchanged - such records are still not applied - only no
	  longer fatal to the connection.

	* wp/fpacwpd.c: do not drop the adjacent session when a deleted record
	  is received for a callsign that is not in the local database.  There
	  is nothing to delete, so the record is now ignored and the session
	  kept instead of calling close_client().  The existence test is also
	  restricted to wp_type_set PDUs, so it is no longer triggered by the
	  union-aliased bytes of other PDU types.

	* wp/wpedit.c: give a clear message when the daemon is not running.
	  wpedit is a client of fpacwpd (it connects through wp_open() and
	  never touches the White Pages file), so it cannot work while the
	  daemon is stopped - the opposite of wpmaint.  When wp_open() fails it
	  now checks whether fpacwpd is running (the same /proc scan used by
	  wpmaint) and prints "the fpacwpd daemon is not running - please start
	  it first" instead of the generic "Cannot open WP service".

	* configure.ac: bump version from 4.1.5-rc15 to 4.1.5-rc16.

 -- Bernard Pidoux <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>  Friday, june 12 2026

	Assisted by Claude Opus 4.8 (Anthropic) <noreply@anthropic.com>.

fpac (4.1.5-rc15)

	* wp/wpmaint.c: refuse to run while the fpacwpd daemon is active.
	  wpmaint rewrites the White Pages file in place, whereas the running
	  daemon keeps it memory-mapped (MAP_SHARED); running both at the same
	  time loses wpmaint's changes and may corrupt the database.  A new
	  fpacwpd_running() helper scans /proc for the daemon, and when it is
	  found wpmaint prints a warning and exits before touching any file.
	  usage() now states that the daemon must be stopped first.

	* wp/db_list.c, wp/wplist.c: let wplist display deleted records.  The
	  server side (db_list_get) no longer skips is_deleted entries, and
	  wplist prints a "Status" column reading DELETED or Ok, so the
	  operator can see records that are pending erasure by wpmaint.

	* lib/libwp.c: fix the wpedit (R)emove command, which never deleted
	  any record.  In ancien() the spurious test "if (days_old < 2)
	  return 1;" rejected every record younger than two days; since
	  wp_set() always stamps the record with the current date, days_old
	  was always 0, so wp_send_pdu() aborted the transmission of the
	  is_deleted PDU (and the receiving decoder rejected it likewise).
	  Removed that test; ancien() again only rejects records older than
	  WP_OBSOLETE (14) days, matching the original behaviour.

	* wp/fpacwpd.c: stop the (R)emove command from being silently reverted
	  on reception.  rose_read_handler() tested whether a deleted record
	  already existed by calling db_get() into the incoming PDU itself,
	  which overwrote the received record (clearing its is_deleted flag and
	  date); db_set() then saw no change and dropped the deletion.  The
	  existence test now uses a separate scratch buffer.

	* wp/db.c, wp/fpacwpd.c: fix the White Pages vector reconciliation
	  between adjacent nodes, which never converged.  db_compute_vector()
	  stopped at the first divergent timeslot (the stop_dirty guard); since
	  slot 0 (the node's own record) diverges permanently it monopolized
	  every exchange and the other slots never reconciled - every divergent
	  slot is now marked dirty.  When sending the dirty batch, a deleted
	  record older than WP_OBSOLETE made wp_send_pdu() fail and the whole
	  batch was aborted as a link error; such records are now skipped (their
	  dirty bit cleared) so the batch completes.

	* lib/libwp.c, lib/wp.h, wp/wpedit.c: print a progress '.' while an
	  interactive client waits for the WP server.  wp_receive_pdu() now
	  polls in one-second slices and emits a dot when the new global
	  wp_progress is set (wpedit sets it, daemons leave it 0), so a slow
	  (R)emove that takes up to WP_API_TIMEOUT no longer looks frozen.

	* lib/wp.h: guard the new "extern int wp_progress" with #ifndef extern.
	  pad/fpad.c does "#define extern" before including the headers to
	  allocate its globals in main; without the guard wp_progress was
	  defined both in fpad.o and in libwp.a, and a full build failed under
	  gcc 12 (-fno-common) with a multiple-definition link error in fpad.

	* scripts/myfpac.in: fix the "Restartting" typo in the restart message.

	* configure.ac: bump version from 4.1.5-rc14 to 4.1.5-rc15.

 -- Bernard Pidoux <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>  Thursday, june 11 2026

	Assisted by Claude Opus 4.8 (Anthropic) <noreply@anthropic.com>.

fpac (4.1.5-rc14)

	* scripts/Makefile.am, scripts/myfpac.in: replace the fpac.sh startup
	  script with myfpac.sh, a reworked version that drives ONLY the FPAC
	  application daemons.  The AX.25 layer (ax0, kissattach, ax25ipd,
	  netromd, beacon, ax25d) is now handled separately by ax25up/ax25stop
	  and is deliberately left untouched, so FPAC can be restarted without
	  bringing down the AX.25 stack.  Adds a stop_proc() helper (TERM, 5 s
	  wait, then KILL), generic template defaults (SYSOP, NODECALL=$HOSTNAME,
	  CONNECT commented out) and DIR=@prefix@/sbin; renames sbin_SCRIPTS,
	  AC_CONFIG_FILES and the man page from fpac.sh to myfpac.sh.

	* etc/Makefile.am, Makefile.am: distribute and install ax25udp.conf.
	  Its template ax25udp.conf.in was present in the tree but was neither
	  substituted, installed nor distributed (missing from etcfiles and
	  EXTRA_DIST), unlike its ax25ipd.conf counterpart.  It is now added to
	  both lists and handled like ax25ipd.conf (substitution, upgrade-safe
	  install, dist).

	* wp/Makefile.am: give the build-only helper make_tab an empty
	  per-target LDADD (make_tab_LDADD =) so it no longer links against
	  ../lib/libfpac.a.  "make dist"/"make distcheck" generate the
	  BUILT_SOURCES (crc_tab.h, produced by make_tab) before the libraries
	  are built; the directory-wide LDADD made make_tab require libfpac.a
	  at that point and dist aborted.  Installed programs are unaffected.

	* Makefile.am, etc/Makefile.am: distribute the *.in source templates
	  consumed by do_subst rather than the generated files.  EXTRA_DIST
	  now ships pathnames.h.in (was pathnames.h) and etc/ax25ipd.conf.in
	  (was ax25ipd.conf); without them the unpacked tarball could not be
	  reconfigured during "make distcheck".  Removed a duplicate
	  ax25ipd.conf entry in etcfiles.

	* Makefile.am: uncomment CLEANFILES = $(pathheader) so the generated
	  pathnames.h is removed by "make clean"/"distclean"; distcleancheck
	  used to fail on this leftover file.

	* Makefile.am: add a distclean-local rule removing autom4te.cache,
	  which "make distclean" previously left behind, so source tarballs
	  are clean without manual cleanup.

	* README: fix typos, drop the obsolete "libax25-0.0.9" TODO entry, and
	  reword the bug-report pointer (GitHub issues, not a mailing list).
	  README.svn rewritten for git and renamed README.git.

	* configure.ac: bump version from 4.1.5-rc13 to 4.1.5-rc14, and switch
	  release archives to xz (AM_INIT_AUTOMAKE dist-xz instead of
	  dist-bzip2) to match the published .tar.xz.

