fpac (4.1.5-rc13)

	* tools/mailbbs.c: fix three bugs causing segmentation faults on nodes
	  where the linfbb BBS application and/or ROSE kernel support are not
	  loaded.

	  1. NULL pointer dereference in AF_ROSE setup (primary segfault cause):
	     rs_get_addr(NULL) reads the ROSE routing table via /proc/net/rose.
	     When the ROSE kernel module is not loaded, read_proc_rs() returns
	     NULL and rs_get_addr() propagates it.  The unguarded call
	     rose_aton(rs_get_addr(NULL), ...) then dereferences NULL.
	     Fix: capture the return value of rs_get_addr() in a local variable,
	     test for NULL, and exit with an explicit diagnostic message before
	     calling rose_aton().

	  2. NULL pointer dereference on local callsign lookup (AF_ROSE,
	     AF_NETROM, AF_AX25): when option -i is not supplied and the
	     port-address lookup (*_config_get_addr()) returns NULL (port not
	     configured), ax25_aton_entry()/ax25_aton() was called with a NULL
	     pointer.
	     Fix: add a NULL check after each *_config_get_addr() call in all
	     three address-family branches, with a diagnostic message directing
	     the user to supply -i.

	  3. Off-by-one buffer overflow in readbbs(): when a received line fills
	     the entire buffer (i == maxlen), nb was set to i+1 (= maxlen+1)
	     instead of i (= maxlen = pos).  In verbose mode the subsequent
	     buffer[nb] = '\0' wrote one or two bytes past the end of the
	     caller's stack buffer (char buf[256]).  Even in the normal \r-
	     terminated case, nb == pos could equal maxlen, making buffer[nb]
	     one byte past the end.
	     Fix (two parts):
	     - Change nb = i+1 to nb = i in the i==maxlen branch so that nb
	       correctly reflects the number of bytes written (== pos).
	     - Change buffer[nb] = '\0' to buffer[pos] = '\0' so the null
	       terminator is always placed at the first unused byte.
	     - Pass sizeof(buf)-1 instead of sizeof(buf) from main() so that
	       maxlen leaves one byte of headroom for the terminator.

	* configure.ac: bump version from 4.1.5-rc12 to 4.1.5-rc13.

-- Bernard Pidoux <bernard.f6bvp@gmail.com>  Tuesday, may 26 2026

fpac (4.1.5-rc12)

	* node/command.c: fix segmentation fault triggered by the sequence
	  "s" (Status) then "u" (Users).

	  do_status() declared a local cfg_t variable that shadowed the
	  global cfg, then called cfg_open() a second time.  That second
	  call leaked all heap memory allocated for the local config
	  (alias/command/node/route linked lists), called dnic_open() again
	  appending duplicate entries to the global dnic_list, and invoked
	  putenv() with a pointer to a stack-local char[256] buffer.  After
	  cfg_open() returned, those five environment-variable pointers
	  became dangling, corrupting the Nodecmds linked list on the next
	  stack reuse and causing cmdparse() to crash on cmdp->name.

	  Fix: remove the local "cfg_t cfg" declaration and the cfg_open()
	  call from do_status().  The global cfg loaded at startup by
	  fpacnode.c is used directly, as it always was for every other
	  command function.

	* node/command.c (do_routes): remove unwanted colour on the DNIC
	  Address column of the "r" (Routes) table.  The field was wrapped
	  in NodeColors.adresse / ResetColor; it is now printed as plain
	  text, consistent with the surrounding route data.

	* node/command.c (do_links): fix uniform green colour applied to
	  the Status column of the "l" (Links) table.  The switch(p->st)
	  block previously assigned only the text label (cp) per state
	  while always using NodeColors.ax25_connected for the colour.
	  A state_color variable is now set alongside cp for each case,
	  mapping the six AX.25 states to the same NodeColors fields used
	  by do_users():
	    0 Disconnected → ax25_disconnected
	    1 Conn pending → ax25_conn_pending
	    2 Disc pending → ax25_disc_pending
	    3 Connected    → ax25_connected
	    4 Recovery     → ax25_recovery
	    default        → ax25_unknown

	* node/colors.h, node/colors.c: new source files implementing a
	runtime-configurable colour system for fpacnode's interactive display.

	  - node_colors_t struct holds one ANSI escape sequence per semantic
	    element (24 fields): version, node, hello, en_tete, indicatif,
	    adresse, port, date, ax25_disconnected, ax25_conn_pending,
	    ax25_disc_pending, ax25_connected, ax25_recovery, ax25_unknown,
	    rose_connected, rose_idle, netrom_connected, netrom_idle,
	    qualite_bonne, qualite_moyenne, qualite_nulle, ind_oui, ind_non.

	  - colors_set_defaults() initialises every field to its built-in
	    ANSI macro (F_*/B_* from node.h), reproducing the rc11 behaviour
	    exactly when no configuration file is present.

	  - read_colors() opens /usr/local/etc/ax25/fpacnode.colors, parses
	    INI-style [section] / key = value lines, maps French colour names
	    (rouge, vert + fond_rouge, …) to ANSI sequences via fg_table[] and
	    bg_table[] lookup arrays, and stores the result in NodeColors.
	    Unknown colour names are silently ignored (default kept).
	    Returns 1 if the file was read, 0 if absent.

	* node/fpacnode.c: add #include "colors.h"; call read_colors()
	immediately after cfg_open() so the palette is ready before any
	output.  Replace hardcoded F_Red/F_Yellow/F_Blue macros in the
	connection banner (version number, hostname, hello/info file) and
	User.call display with NodeColors.version, NodeColors.node,
	NodeColors.hello, NodeColors.indicatif.

	* node/command.c: add #include "colors.h"; replace all 94 hardcoded
	F_*/B_* colour macro occurrences with NodeColors.* references:

	  - Column headers (F_Yellow) → NodeColors.en_tete throughout
	    do_mheard(), do_routes(), do_links(), do_rose(), do_ports(),
	    do_netrom(), do_status(), do_wp() and related helpers.

	  - AX.25 callsigns (F_Green) → NodeColors.indicatif.
	    ROSE/DNIC addresses (F_Green) → NodeColors.adresse.

	  - AX.25 link states in do_links() switch(p->st):
	      case 0 Disconnected  F_Green+B_Red     → ax25_disconnected
	      case 1 Conn pending  F_Yellow+B_Blue   → ax25_conn_pending
	      case 2 Disc pending  F_Yellow+B_Magenta→ ax25_disc_pending
	      case 3 Connected     F_Black+B_Green   → ax25_connected
	      case 4 Recovery      F_Blue+B_Yellow   → ax25_recovery
	      default Unknown      F_White+B_Gray    → ax25_unknown
	    Format strings updated from "%s%s%s%s%s" to "%s%s%s%s" since
	    fg and bg sequences are now stored pre-concatenated in NodeColors.

	  - ROSE circuit states in do_rose() switch(rp->st): same six states
	    mapped to the same ax25_* fields for consistency.

	  - ROSE neighbour state in do_links():
	      Connected   F_Black+B_Green → rose_connected
	      --------- F_Green+B_Red   → rose_idle

	  - NET-ROM neighbour status in do_links():
	      Connected   F_Black+B_Green   → netrom_connected
	      --------- F_Yellow+B_Magenta→ netrom_idle

	  - Route quality in do_stat_file():
	      qual==0     F_Red    → qualite_nulle
	      qual<=50    F_Yellow → qualite_moyenne
	      qual>50     F_Green  → qualite_bonne

	  - Boolean "yes/no" column in do_rose_ckt(): restructured from
	    compile-time string-literal concatenation
	    (F_Black B_Green " yes" ResetColor) to a runtime expression
	    using NodeColors.ind_oui / NodeColors.ind_non; tprintf format
	    string updated accordingly.

	  - "Opened"/"Closed" route indicators → ind_oui / ind_non.

	  - do_status() hostname → NodeColors.node; callsigns →
	    NodeColors.indicatif; DNIC address → NodeColors.adresse;
	    version number → NodeColors.version; build date → NodeColors.node.

	* node/Makefile.am: add colors.c and colors.h to fpacnode_SOURCES.

	* configure.ac: bump version from 4.1.5-rc11 to 4.1.5-rc12.

	* /usr/local/etc/ax25/fpacnode.colors: new configuration file
	installed by generate_colors_conf.py.  Plain-text key=value syntax
	with INI sections; comment field on each line contains the colour name
	rendered as a live ANSI preview for self-documentation.

	* fpacnode_colors.py: Python utility that displays the complete ANSI
	palette (foreground and background) with live colour rendering, plus a
	full preview of all fpacnode.colors settings in their configured colours.

	* generate_colors_conf.py: Python utility that writes (or regenerates)
	/usr/local/etc/ax25/fpacnode.colors with embedded ANSI codes in the
	comment field of each line.  Accepts an optional destination path as
	argument; use "-" to preview on stdout.

