fpac (4.1.5-rc11)

	* node/node.h: fix PERM_TELNET macro — operator '&' replaced by '|';
	the macro always evaluated to zero, making the telnet permission test
	permanently false regardless of the individual flags set.
	Add missing extern declaration for do_manage_routes().

	* node/io.c: fix two bugs in usflush() causing heap buffer overflow
	and silent data corruption:

	  1. When write() returns -1 (e.g. EBADF), the function returned
	     immediately without resetting iop->opointer.  On the next call
	     to rsendchar(), the character was written at obuf[opointer] with
	     opointer >= paclen — one byte past the end of the heap-allocated
	     output buffer.  The overflow corrupts heap metadata and causes a
	     segmentation fault on the subsequent command (reproducible: "ne"
	     followed by "?").  Fix: reset iop->opointer = 0 before returning
	     -1.

	  2. Partial-write handling: after writing ret bytes out of opointer,
	     the remaining data was correctly shifted to the front of the
	     buffer with memmove(), but opointer was then set to ret (bytes
	     already written) instead of opointer - ret (bytes still pending),
	     leading to silent output truncation on slow or flow-controlled
	     links.  Fix: iop->opointer = iop->opointer - ret.

	  Both bugs were confirmed with AddressSanitizer:
	    heap-buffer-overflow — WRITE of size 1, 0 bytes past the end of
	    a 1024-byte region: rsendchar (io.c:202) <- do_netrom (command.c:2472)

	* node/io.c: fix potential buffer overflow in usvprintf() — replace
	vsprintf() with vsnprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), ...) and cap the returned
	length to prevent writing beyond the static buffer.

	* node/command.c: fix do_help() — fname[80] was used uninitialised;
	all three code paths that assemble the help file path now use
	snprintf(fname, sizeof(fname), "%s%s", FPAC_HELP_DIR, ...) so the
	directory prefix is always set correctly.
	Enlarge fname buffer from 80 to 256 bytes to avoid -Wformat-truncation
	with long filenames under FPAC_HELP_DIR.
	Register do_manage_routes() in init_nodecmds() as built-in command
	'MRoutes' (min. 2 chars); the function was defined but never reachable.

	* node/gateway.c: remove all debug node_msg() calls tagged
	"DEBUG F6BVP" from get_address(), connect_to() (AF_ROSE, AF_NETROM,
	AF_AX25 branches) and do_connect(); these messages were emitted on the
	user's terminal during normal operation.
	Clean up invalid-port error message to a user-readable form.
	Fix do_connect(): add wp_opened flag so wp_close() is called in every
	exit path, including early returns for "already connected", argc < 3,
	invalid callsign and "no FlexNet gateway" conditions.
	Fix do_connect(): save original argvp pointer in argvp_base before
	the ++argvp pre-increment passed to connect_to(); add 'done:' label
	at function end for consistent cleanup of all three calloc'd strings
	and the pointer array.
	Remove dead commented-out code blocks in do_connect().

