fpac (4.1.5-rc8)
	* Bug fix: sort_proc_nr_nodes() - infinite loop on large /proc/net/nr_nodes
	The previous bubble sort implementation restarted from the head of the
	list after every swap, causing an O(n²) worst-case complexity and a
	potential infinite loop when duplicate callsigns were present (strcmp
	comparison used <= 0 instead of < 0). Replaced by a qsort()-based
	implementation using a temporary pointer array, giving O(n log n)
	complexity regardless of list size.

	* NetRom command new feature: 'ne' command - new sort order arguments
	'a' : sort nodes list by callsign (alphabetic order)  [existing option]
	'm' : sort nodes list by alias/mnemonic (alphabetic order) [new option]
	Default (no argument) : sort by quality (decreasing order, unchanged)
	Usage: ne [a|m]

